Feature: every unit-suite failure leaves the inventory with a classification and its evidence

  # BL-815 — DRAFT, deliberately not executable.
  #
  # This slice's deliverable is a committed measurement, not new runtime
  # behaviour, so no step handler can drive these scenarios. Shipping them as
  # a live .feature would hand the acceptance runner scenarios with no
  # handlers and hard-fail the hardener's gate for no benefit (BL-233). The
  # real verification is the QA procedure in the ticket.
  #
  # Kept because the shape is the contract: what "classified" has to mean
  # before a failure may leave the inventory.

  Background:
    Given the measured failing set from the 2026-08-05 full-suite run

  # BL-815 classification-requires-isolation-evidence-01
  Scenario Outline: a failure is classified only against a recorded isolation run
    Given a failing test classified as <classification>
    When the evidence file is reviewed
    Then the isolation run result is recorded for that test
    And the host load average at the time of the run is recorded
    And <consequence> is recorded for that test

    Examples:
      | classification         | consequence           |
      | real regression        | a fix ticket id       |
      | real slowdown          | a fix ticket id       |
      | load-induced           | an argued no-fix note |
      | suite-infra            | an argued no-fix note |

  # BL-815 environmental-needs-a-passing-isolated-run-02
  Scenario: calling a failure environmental requires it to pass alone
    Given a failing test classified as load-induced
    When the evidence file is reviewed
    Then that test is recorded as passing when run in isolation
    And the load average of the failing run is recorded as well above the core count

  # BL-815 isolated-failure-is-a-defect-03
  Scenario: a failure that survives isolation is a defect and gets a ticket
    Given a failing test that still fails when run alone on a quiet host
    When the evidence file is reviewed
    Then that test is classified as a real regression
    And a fix ticket id is recorded for it

  # BL-815 no-green-by-budget-04
  Scenario Outline: a budget widened without a measured cause is rejected
    Given the slice changed <artefact>
    And no measured cause is recorded for the change
    When the change is reviewed
    Then the change is rejected

    Examples:
      | artefact             |
      | a per-test timeout   |
      | a skip annotation    |
      | an exclude glob      |

  # BL-815 budget-widened-with-cause-is-allowed-05
  Scenario: a budget widened with a measured cause is allowed
    Given the slice changed a per-test timeout
    And a measured cause is recorded for the change
    When the change is reviewed
    Then the change is accepted

  # BL-815 inventory-is-complete-06
  Scenario: no failure leaves the inventory unexamined
    Given the measured failing set
    When the evidence file is reviewed
    Then every test in the set carries a classification
    And none is recorded as environmental without its isolation evidence
